WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.841
A local model file contains model weights, usually stored as tensors.

00:00:03.841 --> 00:00:09.282
Tensors are structured arrays of numbers that represent what the model learned during training or fine-tuning.

00:00:09.282 --> 00:00:11.663
Those numbers are not useful in isolation.

00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:16.084
The runtime has to know the model architecture, tensor names, tensor shapes, precision,

00:00:16.084 --> 00:00:20.505
and layout so it can map the file contents into the correct computation.

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:24.586
Metadata turns a model file into something a runtime can reason about.

00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:28.327
It can describe architecture information, context length, tokenizer details, quantization type,

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:31.387
special tokens, model family, and sometimes prompt formatting hints.

00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:36.148
This is why a model file is more than a single blob of numbers.

00:00:36.148 --> 00:00:40.229
It is a package of data and instructions that helps the runtime

00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:42.270
load and use the model consistently.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:47.031
Tokenizer data is especially important because models do not process text as raw words.

00:00:47.031 --> 00:00:51.452
Text is broken into tokens, and generated tokens are converted back into text.

00:00:51.452 --> 00:00:56.213
The vocabulary, special tokens, and tokenizer behavior need to match what the model expects.

00:00:56.213 --> 00:00:57.914
If the tokenizer is wrong,

00:00:57.914 --> 00:01:02.335
prompt text may be represented differently than the model was trained to understand,

00:01:02.335 --> 00:01:05.055
which can lead to weak or unexpected output.

00:01:05.055 --> 00:01:08.796
Runtime compatibility depends on both the file and the inference engine.

00:01:08.796 --> 00:01:10.837
A GGUF file may be valid,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:14.918
but an older runtime might not support a newer architecture, metadata field,

00:01:14.918 --> 00:01:15.938
or quantization type.

00:01:15.938 --> 00:01:20.699
Likewise, a runtime may support the architecture but require specific settings to perform well.

00:01:20.699 --> 00:01:24.780
Local inference is a combination of model file, runtime capability, hardware fit,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.460
and configuration.
